hexagon: a switch for the smallest batch of the chunked gated delta net

The cost

A GATED_DELTA_NET batch of fewer than 32 tokens runs on the sequential kernel of gated-delta-net-ops.c.
That kernel reads and writes the full state of each head (128 x 128 floats in VTCM) for each token. In the
op profile of the 4B Q8_0 on the v79 NPU (the stage imgturn, the draft on), a batch of 22 tokens uses
1.15 ms in each of the 24 layers, which is 28 ms of a prefill call of 22 tokens. Version 2 of the chunked
kernel uses 3.4 to 3.6 us for each token at 744 and 1024 tokens (the same profile), thus one chunk of 64
tokens uses approximately 0.23 ms.

The change

- htp-gdn-params.h gives GATED_DELTA_NET the kernel param HTP_GDN_KP_CHUNK_MIN: the smallest number of
  tokens outside the snapshot tail for version 2. The value 0 keeps the limit of the DSP,
  GDN_CH_MIN_TOKENS (32). Version 1 always keeps 32.
- The host gives the value of GGML_HEXAGON_GDN_CHUNK_MIN in the params of each GATED_DELTA_NET op. The
  preset value is 2, and a negative value gives 0. Thus an A/B run needs no other build.
- A batch of fewer than 64 tokens is one partial chunk. gdn_c2_zero_tail sets the rows past the last token
  and their gate and beta to zero, thus they give no term. With the limit of 32, the op of 744 tokens has
  a partial chunk of 40 tokens.
- The limit is 1 or more. Thus a batch with K > 1 snapshot slots keeps one token or more in the chunk
  loop, and the tail writes each of the K slots.
- test-backend-ops gives the HTP backend the bound of the chunked kernel (2e-6) on the shapes that go to
  that kernel. Its predicate reads GGML_HEXAGON_GDN_CHUNK and GGML_HEXAGON_GDN_CHUNK_MIN with the rule of
  the host, thus the cases of 2 to 31 tokens get that bound with the preset values.

The results

The kernel lab (tools/htp-lab, target gdnk with --chunk_min 1, the release flags with -flto, the
functional mode with the HMX, 32 heads of 128, 16 key heads, the L2 norm of q and k in the op, gates from
-0.5 or from -30): the NMSE of the output, of the last state and of the other snapshot slots against a
float64 reference.
    tokens  K  gates   output     state      other slots
    2       1  -0.5    2.02e-07   1.35e-07   -
    3       1  -0.5    2.44e-07   1.77e-07   -
    5       1  -0.5    2.91e-07   2.17e-07   -
    8       1  -0.5    3.02e-07   2.46e-07   -
    16      1  -0.5    3.47e-07   2.65e-07   -
    22      1  -0.5    3.64e-07   2.56e-07   -
    31      1  -0.5    3.54e-07   2.42e-07   -
    5       4  -0.5    6.16e-08   1.16e-08   3.11e-08
    8       4  -0.5    1.65e-07   4.45e-08   9.34e-08
    22      4  -0.5    3.19e-07   6.52e-08   1.42e-07
    8       1  -30     3.31e-07   2.08e-07   -
    22      1  -30     3.06e-07   2.06e-07   -
Each run gives only finite values and is less than the bound of 2e-6. The sequential kernel gives 1.68e-14
and 9.87e-15 at 8 tokens: the chunked kernel has the f16 inputs of the HMX, as at 32 tokens and more. The
simulator gives an exact zero for a qfloat product with a zero operand, and the v79 NPU does not. Thus the
phone stage spf (tools/stages/spf) holds the KL check of the model and the time of each batch size.

